  No exit code or gap count is quoted here on purpose. The audit scans a moving
  `--last 9` window, so both change as the lane works; two successive versions of
  this artifact quoted numbers that were stale by the time a seat checked them.
  A durable claim is the one that does not depend on when it is read.
- **Nothing runs the shell suites automatically.** There is no CI, and
  `make test` is `go test ./...`. `shell-test` gives them one command and one
  obvious place to be listed; it does not make them run. Closing that for real
  needs CI or a hook, and neither is in scope here.
